  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peninsular Malaysias first Conservation K9 Unit to Combat Poaching and Illegal Wildlife Trade of Malayan Tiger and Rhinos</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaysia is a source and transit country for internationally trafficked wildlife products. The Critically Endangered Malayan tiger (Panthera tigris jacksoni) is poached in Malaysia, and rhino horns are trafficked from Africa and Asia through Peninsular Malaysia to countries of demand. Conservation K9 units, the first of its kind in Peninsular Malaysia, composed of one tracking K9 unit to track poachers and snares in tiger habitats, and one detection K9 unit to detect wildlife contraband such as rhino horn and tiger parts at transit points, will increase the number of tiger snares extracted and poachers apprehended, and increase wildlife seizures. Once formed, these K9 units will be available for use to the Department of Wildlife and National Parks, Royal Malaysian Customs Department, global logistics and transport companies as well as local conservation NGOs. Project objectives are to enhance: (1) Effectiveness and efficiency of law enforcement efforts in wildlife trafficking points through the formation of a K9 detection unit; and, (2) Effectiveness and efficiency of law enforcement efforts in tiger habitats through the formation of a K9 tracking unit.</narrative>
  </description>
